  "instance_name": "mapping_001",
  "label": "zombies are mapped as non-human entities to justify homicide classification",
  "description": "The text 'it can't be homicide if there is no race' is mapped onto the visual depiction of zombies. The zombies, being non-human entities in the visual material, are used as an analogy to imply that if victims are not racially defined (i.e., 'non-human'), then their killing cannot be classified as homicide. This creates an analogical mapping where the visual zombies represent dehumanized racial groups (particularly people of color) in the context of racially motivated violence.",
